<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net"><diagram id="p_03_solo_levels" name="03-solo-levels"><mxGraphModel dx="800" dy="600" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1280" pageHeight="820" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0" /><mxCell id="1" parent="0" /><mxCell id="title" value="Three solo levels of realism: the unit is the DEPLOYED SERVICE, not the model - and the gaps between levels are the finding" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#f5f5f5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="12" width="1240" height="30" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="l3" value="L3  -  service WITH its real upstream&#10;answers: how fast is the service on REAL INPUT?&#10;(e.g. the camera service feeding mapping)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="70" width="740" height="470" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="l2" value="L2  -  the service AS DEPLOYED&#10;answers: how fast is the SERVICE?&#10;real container + runtime + pre/post-processing, driven through its own interface" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="120" y="190" width="620" height="320" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="l1" value="L1  -  the engine alone&#10;answers: how fast is the NETWORK?&#10;compiled inference engine timed in isolation&#10;(trtexec-style: no service wrapper, no middleware)&#10;= the floor" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=center;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="190" y="320" width="480" height="160" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="gap21" value="GAP  L2 - L1 = the service's OWN overhead&#10;= the CPU 'glue' (pre/post-processing, container,&#10;runtime) around the bare network. On a small robot&#10;this glue usually dominates (see A2)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;fontSize=12;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="820" y="230" width="420" height="90" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="gap32" value="GAP  L3 - L2 = the cost of REAL UPSTREAM data&#10;= real input shape and timing from the upstream&#10;service it consumes. Captures real-input cost, but&#10;adds the upstream's variability." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;fontSize=12;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="820" y="110" width="420" height="90" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="side_hdr" value="SIDE PANEL: idle floor vs working cost" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=center;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="820" y="340" width="420" height="26" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="idle" value="IDLE FLOOR&#10;an event-driven service&#10;with NO input does almost&#10;nothing (~0 cost).&#10;This is NOT its working&#10;cost. Must be labelled&#10;'idle floor', never&#10;reported as the cost." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="820" y="372" width="200" height="120" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="work" value="WORKING COST&#10;DRIVE the service through&#10;its own API:&#10;- speech plan -&gt; voice&#10;- inject detections -&gt; perception&#10;- replay motion -&gt; mapping&#10;- command a mode -&gt; control&#10;so it does REAL work." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1040" y="372" width="200" height="120" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="guide" value="HOW TO USE (C2):  Measure SOLO before combined - the clean per-service baseline is the DENOMINATOR for the interference factor the combined run reveals (C6); it is a result, not a rehearsal.  Pick the level that answers your question: L1 for the network floor, L2 for the deployable cost, L3 for real-input cost.  Measure the deployed service (L2), not the bare model (L1) - the network is only a fraction of the service's cost.  A 'replaced pair' (sized stand-in) is measured at its level and labelled with its basis, so the combined run adds a known, labelled quantity." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f0f0f0;strokeColor=#999999;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="560" width="1180" height="96" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="legend" value="Legend&#10;Nesting = increasing realism: L1 (engine) within L2 (deployed service) within L3 (+ real upstream)&#10;green = L1 engine   blue = L2 service   purple = L3 upstream&#10;amber = the gap between two levels (what each gap measures)   red = the idle-floor caveat" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="676" width="560" height="76" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="src" value="Source: note C2 (solo runs and levels). L1 = a trtexec-style engine timing (NVIDIA TensorRT, docs.nvidia.com/deeplearning/tensorrt/). 'Idle floor', 'working cost', 'driver', and 'replaced pair' are C2 terms. The interference factor the baseline feeds is defined in C6. No measured robot numbers." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=9;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="640" y="676" width="600" height="76" as="geometry" /></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>